WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.111
- It's kind of interesting
in the gay community

00:00:02.111 --> 00:00:04.708
that we went through so much
profiling in our history

00:00:04.708 --> 00:00:07.017
and yet we are the first
to profile our peers.

00:00:07.017 --> 00:00:09.747
(light ambient music)
- My initial reaction

00:00:09.747 --> 00:00:11.791
when I found out I was HIV positive

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:15.682
was that I was never ever
going to have sex again,

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.054
I was never gonna be in
a relationship again,

00:00:18.054 --> 00:00:20.420
it just was basically over.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.226
And that lasted for quite a while.

00:00:23.226 --> 00:00:26.279
- I didn't know what to do, where to turn,

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:29.101
I didn't think I was ever
gonna be worth dating

00:00:29.101 --> 00:00:31.184
after being HIV positive.

00:00:32.268 --> 00:00:33.435
- It happened.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.352
But I didn't go through
the stress or the angst

00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:42.106
that many people experience,
that many of my friends

00:00:42.106 --> 00:00:44.582
that have become positive
have experienced.

00:00:44.582 --> 00:00:49.222
I attended my first leather
event and I found out

00:00:49.222 --> 00:00:51.420
that the leather community is very open

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.181
and accepting of people that are positive.

00:00:54.181 --> 00:00:58.331
- I got a lot of really
rude, nasty messages online

00:00:58.331 --> 00:01:01.473
from people with no profile pictures,

00:01:01.473 --> 00:01:03.289
no way to identify who they were,

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:06.725
just saying that I'm giving
people AIDS on purpose

00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:10.941
or that I am infecting
people, that I'm going to die,

00:01:10.941 --> 00:01:14.168
that I deserve it because
I'm sexually free,

00:01:14.168 --> 00:01:17.372
or sexually liberated, so I
deserve it, that I'm a slut.

00:01:17.372 --> 00:01:20.018
- On some of these dating
sites they use a phrase

00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:22.108
when they're looking for a certain person,

00:01:22.108 --> 00:01:24.253
they'll say you must be clean,

00:01:24.253 --> 00:01:26.460
so I'm being profiled
as being a dirty person

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.589
because I'm HIV positive, which
is farthest from the truth.

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:33.425
So there's a stigma there for sure.

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:35.362
- It actually really sucks, for instance,

00:01:35.362 --> 00:01:40.227
on Grindr I've been blocked
when I've been open and honest.

00:01:40.227 --> 00:01:43.508
They solely look at your diagnosis,

00:01:43.508 --> 00:01:47.820
categorize you, like
most of us do in America,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.349
put you in a box, and then kind of

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:52.031
shove you off to the side.

00:01:52.031 --> 00:01:54.472
- I was able to have some relationships

00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:56.970
as far as being physical with guys again,

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.027
but the boyfriend thing never happened.

00:02:00.027 --> 00:02:02.415
I've been single since the 80s.

00:02:02.415 --> 00:02:06.582
- To me being HIV positive,
I don't really notice it.

00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:11.113
It's just something that is part of me,

00:02:11.113 --> 00:02:14.618
but I don't think about
it, I take a pill at night,

00:02:14.618 --> 00:02:17.654
and besides going to a
doctor every three months

00:02:17.654 --> 00:02:21.055
to do my blood work,
it's really a non-issue

00:02:21.055 --> 00:02:24.135
for me, it doesn't affect my life.

00:02:24.135 --> 00:02:27.190
- To those of you who
won't open up your heart

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.198
and date someone who is HIV positive,

00:02:30.198 --> 00:02:34.041
you need to open a book or go
to a website just like I did.

00:02:34.041 --> 00:02:36.113
- With the advent of better medications

00:02:36.113 --> 00:02:37.578
for the last eight to 10 years,

00:02:37.578 --> 00:02:40.410
I've been undetectable,
which means that it's almost

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.709
impossible for me to pass on the virus.

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:46.569
So with my undetectable
status and condoms and prep,

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:49.901
that's just a triple layer of protection.

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:53.068
(light ambient music)

00:03:01.393 --> 00:03:03.462
- People are definitely
missing out if they are

00:03:03.462 --> 00:03:06.033
closing themselves off from
anybody who is positive,

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.541
or black, Asian, or feminine.

00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:11.326
You never know what a
person has inside of them

00:03:11.326 --> 00:03:13.369
and how he will surprise
you if you actually

00:03:13.369 --> 00:03:14.837
give him a chance and get to know him.

00:03:14.837 --> 00:03:16.848
You are truly missing out if
you are not meeting somebody

00:03:16.848 --> 00:03:20.515
just because of a
checklist on his profile.

